# RC Detailing Tools

Phone-friendly tools for RC Detailing, hosted on GitHub Pages.

- `index.html` - landing page
- `Vehicle_Inspection.html` - walk-around inspection form with photos and sign-off
- `Analytics_Dashboard.html` - Urable CSV analytics
- `manifest.webmanifest`, `sw.js`, icons - lets the tools install to a phone home screen and work offline

## Publish

1. Create a new GitHub repository (for example `rc-tools`).
2. Upload every file in this folder to the root of the repository.
3. Settings > Pages > Source: **Deploy from a branch**, branch **main**, folder **/ (root)**. Save.
4. After a minute the site is live at `https://<your-username>.github.io/rc-tools/`.

## Update

Replace the changed file and upload again. `sw.js` carries a version stamp; re-upload it too so phones pick up the new files.

// RC Detailing tools: cache-first so the inspection form works without signal.
var CACHE = 'rc-tools-43c156e801';
var FILES = ["index.html", "Vehicle_Inspection.html", "Analytics_Dashboard.html", "manifest.webmanifest", "icon-192.png", "icon-512.png", "apple-touch-icon.png"];
self.addEventListener('install', function(e){ e.waitUntil(caches.open(CACHE).then(function(c){ return c.addAll(FILES); }).then(function(){ return self.skipWaiting(); })); });
self.addEventListener('activate', function(e){ e.waitUntil(caches.keys().then(function(keys){ return Promise.all(keys.filter(function(k){ return k!==CACHE; }).map(function(k){ return caches.delete(k); })); }).then(function(){ return self.clients.claim(); })); });
self.addEventListener('fetch', function(e){ e.respondWith(caches.match(e.request).then(function(r){ return r || fetch(e.request); })); });

